# {project_name} Documentation Policy

## Canonical Ownership

- Repo topology lives in `ORCHESTRATION.md`.
- Task-board command policy lives in `TASKS.md`.
- Domain language lives in `GLOSSARY.md`.
- Slice mapping, behavior contracts, and gates live in `SLICES.md`.
- Runbooks live in their pattern-named docs, one canonical runbook per
  pattern, each routed from `AGENTS.md`.
- Unresolved coordination state lives in `STATUS.md`; link canonical release,
  slice, ticket, and deployment evidence instead of copying their contents.
- Evidence-backed skill-improvement candidates live in `SKILL_FEEDBACK.md`.
- Implementation specs, schemas, migrations, and code-level details live in the
  relevant implementation repo.

## Boundaries

- Do not duplicate canonical glossary terms in repo-local context files.
- Do not turn `TASKS.md` into an issue tracker or status log.
- Coordinators replace status rows by stable ID and remove resolved rows after
  retaining evidence. Workers return evidence without editing the snapshot.
- Reconcile affected rows after landing, deployment, abandonment, a durable
  blocker change, or handoff. Task-board generation remains read-only.
- Do not store credentials in orchestration docs.

## Size Budgets

The validator always rejects `STATUS.md` above 40 lines or 600 words, regardless
of this table or `--strict`. Other line budgets are soft and configurable.

| Doc | Budget |
| --- | --- |
| AGENTS.md | 60 |
| STATUS.md | 40 |
| DOCUMENTATION_POLICY.md | 60 |
| ORCHESTRATION.md | 80 |
| TASKS.md | 80 |
| WORKTREES.md | 80 |
| QA.md | 120 |
| DEBUG.md | 120 |
| DEPLOY.md | 120 |
| GLOSSARY.md | 200 |
| SLICES.md | 300 |
| SKILL_FEEDBACK.md | 200 |

## Grooming

When the user says `groom` or `grm`:

- Report first: line counts vs budgets, duplicated truth, orphan docs, dead
  routes, stale references. Write nothing before approval.
- Keep `AGENTS.md` a router: demote detail to the doc that owns it.
- Archive over delete: move stale content to `archive/` under date-stamped
  names such as `archive/STATUS-2026-07.md`. Deletion needs explicit approval.
- Never route `archive/` from `AGENTS.md`; archived content stays out of the
  precontext path.
- Verify against live repo state before pruning topology or slice entries.
- Preserve stable behavior-contract IDs, observable outcomes, and gate evidence
  when compacting landed slices.
